pullrun version 0.7.9
Run a workload. Accepts either a content-addressed digest (sha256:...)
or an image:tag reference (e.g. alpine:latest) which will be pulled first.

The default backend is "container" on Linux and "vm" on macOS.
Use --backend=vm explicitly on Linux to run inside a Firecracker micro-VM.
The kernel is loaded from ~/.pullrun/kernels/ by default, or from
an OCI image via --kernel-image=<ref>.

Usage:
  pullrun run [IMAGE_REF|DIGEST] [flags]

Flags:
      --allow-inbound strings        Allow inbound port (e.g. 8080)
      --allow-outbound strings       Allow outbound: tcp:host:port
  -a, --attach                       Attach to workload: streams stdout/stderr (vm) or polls for exit code (container)
      --backend string               Backend: container, vm, sandbox (default "container")
      --cmd strings                  Override entrypoint command
      --config strings               Mount a config at /<name> (format: name or name=/custom/path)
      --cpu uint                     CPU millicores (1000 = 1 vCPU) (default 1000)
  -e, --env strings                  Environment variables (KEY=VALUE)
      --health-cmd string            Health check command (e.g. 'curl -f http://localhost:80' or 'ls /tmp/healthy')
      --health-interval uint32       Health check interval (seconds) (default 30)
      --health-retries uint32        Consecutive failures before marking unhealthy (default 3)
      --health-start-period uint32   Grace period before health checks start (seconds)
      --health-timeout uint32        Health check timeout (seconds) (default 30)
  -h, --help                         help for run
      --kernel-image string          OCI reference for the kernel image (optional on macOS when ~/.pullrun/kernels/ has one, e.g. 'pullrun/kernel-asahi:6.19.14')
      --memory uint                  Memory limit in bytes (default 536870912)
      --name string                  Workload name (auto-generated if empty)
      --net string                   Network mode: isolated|host|none|slirp (default "isolated")
      --platform string              Target platform for pull (e.g. linux/amd64, linux/arm64)
  -p, --publish strings              Publish host:container port (e.g. 8080:80, or just 8080)
      --registry string              Registry to pull the workload image from (default: docker.io; use 'localhost:5000' for local registries)
      --restart string               Restart policy: no, on-failure, always, unless-stopped (default "no")
      --secret strings               Mount a secret at /run/secrets/<name> (format: name or name=/custom/path)
  -t, --tty                          Allocate a pseudo-TTY for the workload
  -v, --volume strings               Bind mount (source:destination[:options]), e.g. /host/path:/container/path:ro

Global Flags:
      --direct          Use direct mode (spawn runtime as child) (default true)
      --server string   Control plane address (disables direct mode)
